"[2509.00202v1] From TLinFormer to TConstFormer: The Leap to Constant-Time Transformer Attention: Achieving O(1) Computation and O(1) KV Cache during Autoregressive Inference (https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.00202v1)\nciteturn29793view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.00202v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 163\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Machine Learning\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 29 Aug 2025]\nL9: # Title:From TLinFormer to TConstFormer: The Leap to Constant-Time Transformer Attention: Achieving O(1) Computation and O(1) KV Cache during Autoregressive Inference\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Zhongpan Tang L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled From TLinFormer to TConstFormer: The Leap to Constant-Time Transformer Attention: Achieving O(1) Computation and O(1) KV Cache during Autoregressive Inference, by Zhongpan Tang\nL14: \nL15: cite6†View PDF cite7†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Although the Transformer has become the cornerstone of modern AI, its autoregressive inference suffers from a linearly growing KV Cache and a computational complexity of O(N^2 d), severely hindering its ability to process ultra-long sequences. To overcome this limitation, this paper introduces the TConstFormer architecture, building upon our previous work, TLinFormer. TConstFormer employs an innovative periodic state update mechanism to achieve a truly constant-size O(1) KV Cache.\nL17: The computational complexity of this mechanism is also O(1) in an amortized sense: it performs purely constant-time computations for $k-1$ consecutive steps (e.g., $k=256$) and executes a single linear-time global information synchronization only on the $k$-th step. Theoretical calculations and experimental results demonstrate that TConstFormer exhibits an overwhelming advantage over baseline models in terms of speed, memory efficiency, and overall performance on long-text inference tasks.\nL18: This breakthrough paves the way for efficient and robust streaming language model applications.\nL19: Subjects:  | Machine Learning (cs.LG)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite8†arXiv:2509.00202 [cs.LG]\nL21:    | (or cite9†arXiv:2509.00202v1 [cs.LG] for this version)\nL22:    | cite10†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2509.00202†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Zhongpan Tang [cite11†view email ]\nL26: [v1] Fri, 29 Aug 2025 19:23:35 UTC (116 KB)\nL27: \nL28: Full-text links:\nL29: \nL30: ## Access Paper:\nL31: \nL32: View a PDF of the paper titled From TLinFormer to TConstFormer: The Leap to Constant-Time Transformer Attention: Achieving O(1) Computation and O(1) KV Cache during Autoregressive Inference, by Zhongpan Tang\nL33: \nL34:   * cite6†View PDF L35:   * cite7†HTML (experimental) L36:   * cite12†TeX Source L37: \nL38: cite13†view license L39: ### Current browse context:\nL40: \nL41: cs.LG\nL42: \nL43: cite14†< prev |   cite15†next > L44: \nL45: cite16†new | cite17†recent | cite18†2025-09 L46: \nL47: Change to browse by:\nL48: \nL49: cite19†cs L50: \nL51: ### References & Citations\nL52: \nL53:   * cite20†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L54:   * cite21†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L55:   * cite22†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L56: \nL57: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL58: \nL59: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL60: \nL61: [Button: ×]\nL62: \nL63: loading...\nL64: \nL65: Data provided by:\nL66: \nL67: ### Bookmark\nL68: \nL69: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL70: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL71: \nL72: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL73: \nL74: Bibliographic Explorer (cite23†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.or